  "term": "equivalent form",
  "definition": "In this historical logic usage, an equivalent form is a restatement of a proposition into another wording that has the same logical force. The passage uses it especially for recasting universal and particular propositions into standardized forms so their implications about occurrence or existence can be more clearly seen.",
